{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1852178230/12/des.md\"","aggregated_output":"<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据封闭区域内部的色块数量，从颜色图例中查找对应颜色，用该颜色重绘封闭区域的边框。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格底部有一行颜色图例：从左到右依次排列若干不同颜色的小方块（每个方块为 1×1 像素），它们的位置编号（从左数第 1、2、3…个）对应数字 1、2、3…。\n  - 网格主区域中有若干个由 grey 像素绘制的封闭矩形边框（边框厚度为 1 像素），每个矩形内部散落着若干个不同颜色的单像素色块（色块颜色不固定，可以是任意非背景、非 grey 的颜色）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个 grey 封闭矩形边框，数出其内部包含的非背景色块像素个数 N。\n  - 在底部图例中，找到从左数第 N 个颜色方块，读取其颜色 C。\n  - 将该矩形的 grey 边框像素全部重绘为颜色 C。\n  - 矩形内部的色块保持不变，底部图例行在输出中保留。\n\n- `Key insight`：边框颜色不由边框自身或内部色块的颜色决定，而是由内部色块的数量作为索引去查找图例；解题者需要先发现\"计数→查表\"这一两步映射关系。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将标记像素沿所在通道滑动到交叉口，在交叉口处根据通道来源方向组合生成新颜色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格中有由 grey 像素铺成的十字形或 T 形通道网络（通道宽度为 1 像素），通道在若干位置交叉形成交叉口（交叉口为 grey 像素）。\n  - 在某些通道的末端（死胡同位置）放置了单个彩色像素标记，每个标记颜色不同。同一条通道上最多只有一个标记。\n  - 网格边缘某处有一个颜色混合图例区域：图例由若干行组成，每行包含三个相邻像素——前两个像素分别为两种输入颜色，第三个像素为它们混合后的结果颜色，三者之间无间隔。图例提供了题目中所有可能出现的颜色配对及其混合结果。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 将每个标记像素沿其所在的 grey 通道向交叉口方向滑动，标记在经过的 grey 像素上留下自身颜色的轨迹（将 grey 改为标记颜色）。\n  - 标记到达交叉口时停止。\n  - 如果一个交叉口恰好有两个标记从不同方向到达，则该交叉口像素被填充为图例中这两种颜色混合后的结果颜色。\n  - 如果一个交叉口只有一个标记到达，则该交叉口像素填充为该标记的颜色。\n  - 没有标记到达的交叉口保持 grey。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者必须完成三层推理：（1）识别通道拓扑，判断每个标记滑向哪个交叉口；（2）确定哪些交叉口会有双标记汇合；（3）从图例中学习颜色混合规则，预测汇合点的输出颜色。滑动轨迹和混合查表共同构成多层推理链。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据每个房间内地板图案的对称性类型，从图例中查找对应颜色，用该颜色填充该房间墙壁上的门洞像素。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格中有若干由 grey 墙壁像素围成的封闭矩形\"房间\"，每个房间的墙壁上恰好有一个 1 像素宽的缺口（门洞），门洞处为背景色。\n  - 每个房间内部有一个由某种非背景、非 grey 颜色绘制的小图案（地板图案），图案占据房间内部的部分像素。\n  - 网格的左上角有一个颜色-对称性图例区域：图例由 3 行组成，每行左侧是一个 1×1 颜色方块，右侧紧邻一个 3×3 的示意图案（用 maroon 像素在 black 背景上绘制）。三行分别对应三种对称性类型——第一行的示意图案具有左右镜像对称性，第二行的示意图案具有上下镜像对称性，第三行的示意图案仅具有 180° 旋转对称性而不具备单轴镜像对称。每行左侧的颜色方块即为该对称类型对应的填充颜色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个房间，分析其内部地板图案在该房间边界框内的对称性类型。\n  - 如果地板图案具有水平镜像对称性（左右对称），则该房间属于第一类。\n  - 如果地板图案具有垂直镜像对称性（上下对称），则该房间属于第二类。\n  - 如果地板图案仅具有 180° 旋转对称性，则该房间属于第三类。\n  - 在图例中查找该对称类型对应的颜色，将该房间墙壁上的门洞像素填充为该颜色。\n  - 房间内部图案和墙壁保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先从图例区的示意图案归纳出\"颜色对应对称性类型\"的映射规则，再对每个房间独立判断其图案的对称性——两步推理缺一不可，且对称性判断需要视觉旋转/翻转的心理操作。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据种子像素的邻域构型从样板区复制对应的贴图块，在主画布上逐步生长出完整图案。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格被一条垂直的 maroon 分隔线分为左右两个区域。\n  - 左侧为\"样板区\"：包含若干个 3×3 的彩色图案块（图案块之间垂直间隔至少 1 行背景色），每个图案块下方紧贴一个 1×3 的标签行。标签行由 3 个像素组成，其中部分像素被染成 green、其余为 grey。染色位置编码了一个方向模式——左格为 green 代表\"左邻有已有像素\"，中格为 green 代表\"上邻有已有像素\"，右格为 green 代表\"右邻有已有像素\"。\n  - 右侧为\"主画布\"：背景上散布着若干个孤立的 green 单像素种子，种子之间距离足以容纳 3×3 图案块而不重叠。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 按从上到下、从左到右的顺序逐个处理主画布上的 green 种子像素。\n  - 对当前种子，检查其左、上、右三个相邻位置是否存在非背景像素（包括其他 green 种子或之前步骤中已生成的图案像素），得到一个邻域构型。\n  - 将该邻域构型与样板区各标签行的 green 位置组合进行匹配，找到唯一匹配的样板图案块。\n  - 将匹配到的 3×3 图案以种子像素为中心覆盖到主画布上。\n  - 每个种子处理后其输出像素立即生效，影响后续种子的邻域判断。\n  - 输出仅包含主画布区域（裁去分隔线及样板区），尺寸与右侧画布相同。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先破解样板区标签行的方向编码规则（green 位置对应哪些邻域方向），再理解种子按固定顺序处理时的级联效应——前序种子生成的图案会改变后续种子的邻域构型，从而选择不同的样板块。编码解读和顺序依赖分别构成两层独立的推理。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：识别网格中每个色块的形状类别，将同类色块收集到对应的容器框中，容器内按色块面积从小到大排列。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格中散布着若干个单色四连通块（色块），颜色各异，形状各异但可归为三类：矩形类（整个连通块恰好填满其最小外接矩形，包括正方形）、L 形类（由两个不重叠的轴对齐矩形拼接成直角形状，连通块像素数严格小于其外接矩形面积，且从外接矩形中恰好挖去了一个角落矩形）、十字形类（从外接矩形的四个角各挖去一个相同大小的小方块后剩余的形状）。\n  - 网格底部水平排列着三个空的矩形\"容器框\"，每个容器框用不同颜色的 1 像素厚边框绘制（如 red 边框、blue 边框、green 边框），框内为背景色。\n  - 每个容器框内部的左上角有一个由 grey 像素绘制的微型示意图（约 3×3 到 4×4 像素），分别描绘了一个微型矩形轮廓、一个微型 L 形轮廓、一个微型十字形轮廓，表明该容器接收哪类形状。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个散落的色块，判断它属于矩形类、L 形类还是十字形类（判断依据为连通块与其外接矩形的关系）。\n  - 将同类色块收集到对应容器框中。\n  - 在容器框内，色块按像素面积从小到大、从左到右排列（保持色块原始形状和颜色，不做缩放）。相邻色块之间水平间隔 1 像素，所有色块底部对齐到容器框底边内侧。\n  - 色块放入后覆盖容器内原有的 grey 示意图。\n  - 擦除色块在原始位置的像素（还原为背景色）。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要两步非平凡推理：（1）从容器内的微型 grey 示意图归纳出三种形状分类标准（矩形 vs L 形 vs 十字形），这要求在极小像素尺度下识别轮廓特征；（2）发现容器内的排列顺序由面积决定而非颜色或原始位置。分类规则和排序规则分别构成独立的推理层。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将每个彩色线段平移嵌入到边框标尺的对应刻度区间内，线段长度与刻度间距一一匹配。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格左侧边缘内侧第 2 列上有一把垂直的\"刻度标尺\"：由一条连续的 grey 像素竖线构成，标尺上等间隔地嵌有若干不同颜色的单像素刻度标记（刻度标记替换了该位置的 grey 像素）。相邻刻度标记之间的间距各不相同（间距值为 2、3、4、5 等小整数，这里间距指两个刻度之间 grey 像素的数量加 1）。\n  - 网格内部（标尺右侧区域）散布着若干条水平的彩色线段（每条线段为单一颜色的连续水平像素），每条线段的颜色与标尺上的某个刻度标记颜色相同。每种颜色恰好出现一条线段和一个刻度标记。\n  - 每条线段的像素长度恰好等于其同色刻度标记与该标记上方相邻刻度标记之间的间距值。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每条彩色线段，找到标尺上同色的刻度标记。\n  - 确定该刻度标记与其上方相邻刻度标记之间的间距 D（D 等于线段长度）。\n  - 将线段从原位置擦除（还原为背景色）。\n  - 在标尺上，从该颜色刻度标记位置开始、向上方相邻刻度方向，将两刻度之间的 grey 像素全部重绘为该线段颜色，恰好填满两个刻度之间的区间（不覆盖刻度标记本身）。\n  - 标尺上未被线段填充的 grey 像素保持不变，刻度标记像素保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现线段长度与刻度间距之间的数值对应关系来确认颜色匹配，再推断出线段应被\"嵌入\"到标尺的对应刻度区间内——长度既是匹配的验证键又是几何放置的约束条件，这一双重角色是题目的核心隐蔽点。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：每个封闭围栏内的物体沿围栏缺口方向弹射出去，飞行距离由物体面积决定，落点处保留物体形状。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格中有若干个由 orange 像素绘制的矩形\"围栏\"（1 像素厚的空心矩形边框），每个围栏的某一条边上有一个 1 像素宽的缺口。\n  - 每个围栏内部有一个由某种非背景、非 orange 颜色绘制的小型连通块\"物体\"，物体完全包含在围栏内部。\n  - 不同围栏内的物体颜色和形状各不相同。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个围栏，确定缺口所在的边以及缺口的朝向（上、下、左、右四个方向之一）。\n  - 数出围栏内物体的像素面积 N。\n  - 将物体从围栏内擦除（还原为背景色），然后沿缺口朝向平移物体，平移距离为 N 个像素（物体整体移动 N 格）。\n  - 在新位置绘制物体（保持原始形状和颜色）。如果物体移出网格边界，则仅绘制仍在网格内的部分。\n  - 围栏本身（包括缺口）保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：缺口方向决定弹射方向是第一层视觉直觉，但飞行距离由物体自身面积决定是第二层需要归纳的规则——解题者必须注意到不同物体的位移量与其像素数恰好一致，才能完整推断变换。\n</new_puzzle>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfiles = [\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b7bacbf.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/963c33f8.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/332f06d7.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/9385bd28.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/e3721c99.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/3e6067c3.py',\n]\nfor path in files:\n    txt = Path(path).read_text()\n    print(f'===== {path} =====')\n    for fn in ['def main', 'def generate_input']:\n        idx = txt.index(fn)\n        end = txt.find('\\\\ndef ', idx + 1)\n        if end == -1:\n            end = len(txt)\n        # extend until next top-level def after current one; for main this may include helper nested in between? keep manageable\n        snippet = txt[idx:end]\n        lines = snippet.splitlines()\n        print('\\\\n'.join(lines[:90]))\n        print('--- SNIP ---')\n    print()\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfiles = [\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b7bacbf.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/963c33f8.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/332f06d7.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/9385bd28.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/e3721c99.py',\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/3e6067c3.py',\n]\nfor path in files:\n    txt = Path(path).read_text()\n    print(f'===== {path} =====')\n    for fn in ['def main', 'def generate_input']:\n        idx = txt.index(fn)\n        end = txt.find('\\\\ndef ', idx + 1)\n        if end == -1:\n            end = len(txt)\n        # extend until next top-level def after current one; for main this may include helper nested in between? keep manageable\n        snippet = txt[idx:end]\n        lines = snippet.splitlines()\n        print('\\\\n'.join(lines[:90]))\n        print('--- SNIP ---')\n    print()\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b7bacbf.py =====\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Fill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n\n    Input structure:\n    - bg = most common color.\n    - Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n    - Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n\n    Rule:\n    - Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n    - Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n    - Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n\n    Key insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.\n    \"\"\"\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n    h, w = g.shape\n    bg = get_bg(g)\n\n    out = g.copy()\n\n    # Precompute background regions (4-connected). Exclude those containing background corners as \"outside\".\n    bg_comps = _components_mask(g == bg, conn8=False)\n    regions = []  # list of (set_pts, boundary_set, touches_border, size)\n    for pts in bg_comps:\n        region = set(pts)\n        touches = _touches_border(pts, h, w)\n        boundary = set()\n        for r, c in region:\n            for nr, nc in neighbors4(r, c):\n                if 0 <= nr < h and 0 <= nc < w and (nr, nc) not in region and int(g[nr, nc]) != bg:\n                    boundary.add((nr, nc))\n        regions.append((region, boundary, touches, len(region)))\n\n    corners = {(0, 0), (0, w - 1), (h - 1, 0), (h - 1, w - 1)}\n    outside_idxs = set()\n    for i, (reg, _, _, _) in enumerate(regions):\n        if any(p in reg for p in corners if int(g[p]) == bg):\n            outside_idxs.add(i)\n\n    cavities = []\n    for i, (reg, bnd, _, _) in enumerate(regions):\n        if i in outside_idxs or not bnd:\n            continue\n        bcols = {int(g[p]) for p in bnd}\n        cavities.append((reg, bnd, bcols))\n\n    for sr, sc in _seed_pixels(g, bg):\n        seed_col = int(g[sr, sc])\n\n        neigh_cols = []\n        for nr, nc in neighbors4(sr, sc):\n            if 0 <= nr < h and 0 <= nc < w:\n                v = int(g[nr, nc])\n                if v != bg:\n                    neigh_cols.append(v)\n        assert neigh_cols, \"seed pixel must have at least one non-bg neighbor\"\n        line_col = Counter(neigh_cols).most_common(1)[0][0]\n\n        # Trace the connected \"drawing\" reachable from the seed (8-connected, non-background).\n        traced = _nonbg_component8_from(g, (sr, sc), bg)\n\n        for cav, boundary, bcols in cavities:\n            if len(bcols) != 1:\n                continue\n            boundary_in_traced = boundary & traced\n            if not boundary_in_traced:\n                continue\n\n            # Require that the traced boundary is adjacent (8-neigh) to at least one pixel of the line color.\n            # This prevents filling regions that are only connected through other structures, not the line itself.\n            ok = False\n            for r, c in boundary_in_traced:\n                for nr, nc in neighbors8(r, c):\n                    if 0 <= nr < h and 0 <= nc < w and int(g[nr, nc]) == line_col:\n                        ok = True\n                        break\n                if ok:\n                    break\n            if not ok:\n                continue\n\n            for r, c in cav:\n                if int(out[r, c]) == bg:\n                    out[r, c] = seed_col\n\n    return out\n\n# --------------- generator (attempt_1_distractor_network) ---------------\n--- SNIP ---\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n    rng = random.Random()\n    for _ in range(GEN_RETRIES):\n        g = _gen_attempt(rng)\n        if g is not None:\n            return g\n    raise RuntimeError(\"generate_input: exhausted attempts\")\n--- SNIP ---\n\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/963c33f8.py =====\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Drop the columns of the top marker downward, stopping blue-ended columns on grey obstacles and letting maroon-ended columns pass to the bottom.\n\n    Input structure\n    - The background is the dominant color.\n    - The most numerous non-background color forms stationary grey obstacle pixels.\n    - The other two colors form a single 3x3 top-edge marker whose top two rows\n      are maroon and whose bottom row contains maroon or blue control pixels.\n\n    Rule\n    - Erase the top marker.\n    - Treat each marker column as a vertical drop retaining its three colors.\n    - A column whose bottom control pixel is blue stops immediately above the\n      first grey pixel below that column, or bottom-aligns if none exists.\n    - Contiguous maroon-ended columns pass through obstacles and bottom-align;\n      if such a run has a clear down-right slide from a grey ledge, shift the\n      run one column right before bottom-aligning.\n    - When a maroon-ended drop lands through a grey bar on the bottom edge, clear\n      the rest of the marker-width gap in that bottom bar.\n\n    Key insight\n    - The bottom row of the top marker is a control strip: blue cells mean\n      \"stick to the first obstacle,\" while maroon cells mean \"fall through.\"\n    \"\"\"\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n    H = g.shape[0]\n    bg = int(get_bg(g))\n\n    non_bg = colors_present(g, exclude={bg})\n    assert len(non_bg) == 3, \"expected obstacle color plus two marker colors\"\n    obstacle = _unique_largest_count_color(g, non_bg)\n    marker_colors = [color for color in non_bg if color != obstacle]\n    assert len(marker_colors) == 2, \"expected exactly two marker colors\"\n\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = _marker_bbox(g, marker_colors)\n    marker = g[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1]\n    marker_h, marker_w = marker.shape\n    assert (marker_h, marker_w) == (3, 3), \"expected a 3x3 marker\"\n    assert np.all(np.isin(marker, marker_colors)), \"marker bbox must contain only marker colors\"\n\n    pass_color = int(marker[0, 0])\n    assert np.all(marker[:2, :] == pass_color), \"top two marker rows must be the pass-through color\"\n    stop_colors = [color for color in marker_colors if color != pass_color]\n    assert len(stop_colors) == 1, \"expected one stop color\"\n    stop_color = stop_colors[0]\n\n    out = g.copy()\n    out[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1] = bg\n    base = out.copy()\n\n    pass_columns: list[int] = []\n    for j in range(marker_w):\n        c = c0 + j\n        stack = marker[:, j]\n        bottom_control = int(stack[-1])\n\n        if bottom_control == stop_color:\n            obstacles_below = np.flatnonzero(base[r1 + 1 :, c] == obstacle)\n            if len(obstacles_below):\n                floor_r = int(r1 + 1 + obstacles_below[0])\n                top_r = floor_r - marker_h\n            else:\n                top_r = H - marker_h\n            assert top_r >= 0, \"stopped column must fit above its obstacle\"\n            out[top_r : top_r + marker_h, c] = stack\n        else:\n            assert bottom_control == pass_color, \"bottom control must be one of the marker colors\"\n            pass_columns.append(j)\n\n    for start_j, end_j in _runs(pass_columns):\n        source_cols = list(range(c0 + start_j, c0 + end_j + 1))\n        shift = 1 if _can_slide_right(base, obstacle, bg, source_cols, r1, marker_h) else 0\n        top_r = H - marker_h\n\n        for j in range(start_j, end_j + 1):\n            c = c0 + j + shift\n            _clear_bottom_edge_gap(base, out, obstacle, bg, c, marker_w)\n            out[top_r : top_r + marker_h, c] = marker[:, j]\n\n    return out\n\n# --------------- generator (att1) ---------------\n\nGEN_BG, GEN_OBSTACLE, GEN_PASS, GEN_STOP = 7, 5, 9, 1\nGRID_SIZE_RANGE = (14, 16)\nMARKER_SIZE = 3\nSTOP_COUNT_RANGE = (1, 3)\nOBSTACLE_COMPONENT_RANGE = (7, 9)\nOBSTACLE_PIXEL_RANGE = (20, 31)\nCOMPONENT_SIZE_RANGE = (1, 11)\n--- SNIP ---\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n    for _ in range(GENERATION_ATTEMPTS):\n        result = _gen_attempt()\n        if result is not None:\n            return result\n    raise RuntimeError(f\"Failed to generate valid input after {GENERATION_ATTEMPTS} attempts\")\n--- SNIP ---\n\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/332f06d7.py =====\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Slide a solid square through a winding channel to reach a same-sized target square.\n\n    Input structure:\n    - bg (most common color). A river color forms a winding corridor.\n    - Two same-sized NxN solid squares on the river: mover and destination, each a distinct color.\n\n    Rule:\n    - The mover square travels along the river toward the destination.\n    - It can only pass through positions where the full NxN area is river.\n    - If reachable, the mover replaces the destination; otherwise it stops at the farthest reachable point.\n    - The mover's original position is filled with the river color.\n\n    Key insight: Chokepoints narrower than N pixels block the square, forcing it to stop short.\n    \"\"\"\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\n    H, W = g.shape\n\n    # Corner-majority background (more stable than global mode here).\n    bg = int(Counter([int(g[0, 0]), int(g[0, -1]), int(g[-1, 0]), int(g[-1, -1])]).most_common(1)[0][0])\n\n    # Detect solid square components (excluding bg).\n    squares: list[dict] = []\n    for comp in find_components(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4, monochromatic=True, return_format=\"dict\"):\n        col = int(comp[\"color\"])\n        b = comp[\"bbox\"]\n        if bbox_h(b) != bbox_w(b):\n            continue\n        patch = g[int(b[0]) : int(b[2]) + 1, int(b[1]) : int(b[3]) + 1]\n        if not bool((patch == int(col)).all()):\n            continue\n        squares.append({\"col\": int(col), \"r0\": int(b[0]), \"c0\": int(b[1]), \"n\": int(bbox_h(b))})\n\n    assert not (len(squares) < 2)\n\n    # Choose the size that appears at least twice (most common size).\n    by_n: dict[int, list[dict]] = defaultdict(list)\n    for s in squares:\n        by_n[int(s[\"n\"])].append(s)\n    nside = max(by_n.items(), key=lambda kv: (len(kv[1]), kv[0]))[0]\n    cand = by_n[int(nside)]\n    assert not (len(cand) < 2)\n\n    cand.sort(key=lambda s: int(s[\"col\"]))\n    mover = cand[0]\n    dest = cand[1]\n\n    n = int(mover[\"n\"])\n    sr, sc = int(mover[\"r0\"]), int(mover[\"c0\"])\n    dr, dc = int(dest[\"r0\"]), int(dest[\"c0\"])\n\n    # River = most common remaining color (excluding bg and the two square colors).\n    counts = Counter(map(int, g.flatten()))\n    river = None\n    for col, _ct in counts.most_common():\n        if int(col) == int(bg):\n            continue\n        if int(col) in (int(mover[\"col\"]), int(dest[\"col\"])):\n            continue\n        river = int(col)\n        break\n    assert not (river is None)\n\n    trav = (g ==